  "question": {
    "text": "The electric field in an electromagnetic wave is given as<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#969;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math> are angular frequency and velocity of electromagnetic wave respectively. The energy contained in a volume of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;will be<br />(Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>85</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)"
